IMPORT prelude

-- Human Organ Transplant Act 1987 (Singapore) -- which organs the Act reaches (s 2, First and Second Schedules), removal of organs
-- after death and its bars (ss 4, 5), priority of non-objectors as recipients (s 11), the ban on trading in organs and blood and its
-- exemptions (s 13), living donor transplants and transplant ethics committees (ss 15, 16, 17), and confidentiality of donors and
-- recipients (s 28).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HOTA1987.txt. The cover says
-- it "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the body also shows later amendments, the latest annotated
-- being Act 19 of 2025 (in force 5 December 2025, definition of "licensee") and Act 31 of 2023 (in force 1 December 2025, s 4(3)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a donor, a family, a hospital
-- or a would-be buyer or broker meets. Not encoded: the register machinery (ss 8-10, beyond their effect in ss 4 and 11), the
-- recipient-selection committee (s 12), the Director-General's directions (s 18), enforcement powers and informers (ss 19-25), the
-- s 26 carve-outs, offences by bodies corporate (s 29), composition (s 30, up to $2,000), advertising (s 14), and regulations.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Organ Transplant Act 1987 -- transplants`

§§ `2 and the Schedules -- which organs`

-- s 2: "organ" means "(a) except as provided in paragraph (b), any organ of a human body specified in the First Schedule; and (b) for
-- the purposes of Parts 4 and 4A, any organ of a human body". "specified organ" means an organ in the Second Schedule.
-- First Schedule: (1) the kidney (2) the liver (3) the heart (4) the cornea.
-- Second Schedule (specified organs, Part 4A): (1) the kidney (2) "Any part of the liver".
-- So Part 2 (removal after death) reaches only four organs, while the trading ban in Part 4 reaches every organ.
DECLARE Organ IS ONE OF
    `a kidney`
    `a liver or part of one`
    `a heart`
    `a cornea`
    `a lung`

GIVEN `the organ` IS AN Organ
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2 reaches the organ` IF
    CONSIDER `the organ`
    WHEN `a lung` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the organ` IS AN Organ
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the organ is a specified organ` IF
    CONSIDER `the organ`
    WHEN `a kidney` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a liver or part of one` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the organ` IS AN Organ
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the trading ban reaches the organ` IF TRUE

§§ `4, 5 -- removal after death`

-- s 4(1): the designated officer of a hospital "may ... authorise, in writing, the removal of any organ from the body of a person
-- who has died in the hospital" for transplantation to a living person.
-- (2) No authority for a deceased person (a) who in life "registered his or her objection with the Director-General"; (b) "who is
-- neither a citizen nor a permanent resident of Singapore"; (c) "who is below 21 years of age unless the deceased person's parent or
-- guardian has consented"; or (d) whom the officer has reason to believe was mentally disordered, unless a parent or guardian has
-- consented.
-- s 5(1): where the Coroner has jurisdiction to hold an inquest, the officer "must not authorise the removal ... unless the Coroner
-- has given the Coroner's consent". (3) Consent may be oral, confirmed in writing.
-- The default is removal: nothing in s 4 asks for the family's consent for an adult citizen or PR who did not object.
DECLARE Deceased HAS
    `died in the hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered an objection for that organ` IS A BOOLEAN
    `citizen or permanent resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `believed mentally disordered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `parent or guardian consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Coroner has jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Coroner consented` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the deceased` IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a parent's consent is needed` IF
        `the deceased`'s `age` LESS THAN 21
    OR  `the deceased`'s `believed mentally disordered`

GIVEN `the organ` IS AN Organ, `the deceased` IS A Deceased
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `removal after death may be authorised` IF
        `Part 2 reaches the organ` `the organ`
    AND `the deceased`'s `died in the hospital`
    AND (NOT `the deceased`'s `registered an objection for that organ`)
    AND `the deceased`'s `citizen or permanent resident`
    AND ((NOT `a parent's consent is needed` `the deceased`) OR `the deceased`'s `parent or guardian consented`)
    AND ((NOT `the deceased`'s `Coroner has jurisdiction`) OR `the deceased`'s `Coroner consented`)

§§ `11 -- priority as a recipient`

-- s 11: in selecting a recipient of an organ removed under s 4, (a) a person who has not registered an objection for that organ
-- "has priority over a person who has registered such objection"; (b) a person who withdrew an objection has the same priority as a
-- non-objector "at the expiry of 2 years from the date of receipt of the withdrawal by the Director-General provided the person has
-- not registered again any such objection since that date".
GIVEN `ever registered an objection` IS A BOOLEAN, `withdrew it` IS A BOOLEAN, `years since withdrawal received` IS A NUMBER,
      `registered again since` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has the priority of a non-objector` IF
        NOT `ever registered an objection`
    OR  (`withdrew it` AND `years since withdrawal received` AT LEAST 2 AND (NOT `registered again since`))

§§ `13 -- trading in organs and blood`

-- s 13(1): a contract or arrangement under which a person agrees, "for valuable consideration", to the sale or supply of any organ or
-- blood from his or her own body or another's, before or after death, "is void". (2) A party commits an offence: $10,000 or 12 months.
-- (4) (1) and (3) do not apply to (a) reimbursement only of expenses necessarily incurred in removing blood; (b) a Government scheme
-- of medical benefits or privileges for donors and their families or nominees; (c) defraying or reimbursing reasonable costs of
-- removal, transport, preparation, preservation, quality control or storage; costs (including travel, accommodation, domestic help,
-- child care) or loss of earnings attributable to supplying an organ; and short- or long-term medical care or insurance.
-- (5) The Minister may declare classes of processed products outside (1) and (3).
-- (8) A living donor's donation in return for (a) a donation to a recipient of the donor's choice or (b) priority for that recipient
-- "does not, of itself, constitute valuable consideration if the donors have given their consent and the provisions of Part 4A (as
-- applicable) are complied with".
DECLARE Consideration IS ONE OF
    `a cash price`
    `a gift of property`
    `reimbursement of travel, child care and lost earnings`
    `costs of removing, transporting and storing the organ`
    `medical care or insurance after donation`
    `a Government donor benefits scheme`
    `a reciprocal donation to the donor's chosen recipient`
    `priority for the donor's chosen recipient`

GIVEN `the consideration` IS A Consideration, `donors consented and Part 4A complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consideration is exempt` IF
    CONSIDER `the consideration`
    WHEN `a cash price` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a gift of property` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a reciprocal donation to the donor's chosen recipient` THEN `donors consented and Part 4A complied with`
    WHEN `priority for the donor's chosen recipient` THEN `donors consented and Part 4A complied with`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the consideration` IS A Consideration, `donors consented and Part 4A complied with` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a declared class of processed product` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrangement is void` IF
        (NOT `the consideration is exempt` `the consideration` `donors consented and Part 4A complied with`)
    AND (NOT `a declared class of processed product`)

-- s 13(3): $100,000 or 10 YEARS for anyone who (a) gives or offers consideration for an organ "from the body of another person other
-- than for the purpose of transplantation to his or her body"; (b) receives consideration for an organ from the body of another
-- person; (c) offers to sell or supply an organ from the body of another person; (d) initiates or negotiates such a deal, other than
-- for transplantation to his or her own body; (e) takes part in managing a body whose activities include (d).
-- A seller of his or her OWN organ, and a recipient buying for his or her OWN transplant, fall outside (3) and face only s 13(2):
-- $10,000 or 12 months. (On non-exempt consideration; the encoding takes the highest maximum that applies.)
DECLARE TradingRole IS ONE OF
    `a donor selling own organ`
    `a patient buying an organ for own transplant`
    `a buyer of an organ for someone else`
    `a middleman taking a fee`
    `a seller of another person's organ`
    `a manager of an organ-brokering company`

GIVEN `the role` IS A TradingRole
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the role is a trafficking offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `a donor selling own organ` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a patient buying an organ for own transplant` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the role` IS A TradingRole
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for trading` MEANS
    IF `the role is a trafficking offence` `the role` THEN 100000 ELSE 10000

GIVEN `the role` IS A TradingRole
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for trading` MEANS
    IF `the role is a trafficking offence` `the role` THEN 120 ELSE 12

§§ `15, 16, 17 -- living donors`

-- s 15(1): no living donor organ transplant unless (a) "the specified organ is removed in a hospital with the written authorisation of
-- the transplant ethics committee of the hospital"; and (b) the donor has consented and "has not revoked or withdrawn the consent".
-- (4) $10,000 or 12 months.
-- s 17(2): until a Director-General's direction under s 17(1) is complied with, no authorised living donor transplant may be carried
-- out in the hospital "unless otherwise allowed by the Director-General". (4) $10,000 or 12 months.
-- "living donor organ transplant" (s 2) is removal of a SPECIFIED organ (kidney or part of a liver). Inference, not stated: removal of
-- any other organ from a living donor is outside Part 4A altogether, so s 15 does not govern it.
DECLARE LivingTransplant HAS
    `in a hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
    `committee's written authorisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `donor consent standing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a section 17 direction outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Director-General allowed it` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the organ` IS AN Organ, `the transplant` IS A LivingTransplant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the living donor transplant is lawful` IF
        NOT `the organ is a specified organ` `the organ`
    OR  (    `the transplant`'s `in a hospital`
         AND `the transplant`'s `committee's written authorisation`
         AND `the transplant`'s `donor consent standing`
         AND ((NOT `the transplant`'s `a section 17 direction outstanding`) OR `the transplant`'s `Director-General allowed it`))

-- s 15(2): the committee "must not give any authorisation ... unless it is satisfied that" (a) the donor consented; (b) the donor "is
-- not mentally disordered and, despite the person's age, is able to understand the nature and consequence" of the procedures; (c) the
-- consent (i) is not given under a contract or arrangement prohibited by s 13 and (ii) is not obtained "by virtue of any fraud, duress
-- or undue influence". There is no minimum age: the test is understanding, "despite the person's age".
DECLARE Donor HAS
    `consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `mentally disordered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `understands the procedure and its consequences` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consent given under a prohibited deal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `consent tainted by fraud, duress or undue influence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the donor` IS A Donor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee may authorise` IF
        `the donor`'s `consented`
    AND (NOT `the donor`'s `mentally disordered`)
    AND `the donor`'s `understands the procedure and its consequences`
    AND (NOT `the donor`'s `consent given under a prohibited deal`)
    AND (NOT `the donor`'s `consent tainted by fraud, duress or undue influence`)

-- s 16(2): every transplant ethics committee "must consist of not less than 3 persons", of whom (a) at least one a medical
-- practitioner "not employed by or otherwise connected with the hospital"; and (b) at least one a lay person.
GIVEN `members` IS A NUMBER, `independent doctors` IS A NUMBER, `lay persons` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee is properly constituted` IF
        `members` AT LEAST 3
    AND `independent doctors` AT LEAST 1
    AND `lay persons` AT LEAST 1

§§ `28 -- confidentiality`

-- s 28(1): no one may disclose information whereby the identity of a donor, a person about whom a consent or authority was given, or
-- a recipient "may become publicly known". (2) Except information disclosed (a) to administer and enforce the Act; (b) to refer a
-- complaint about a medical practitioner under s 39(1) of the Medical Registration Act 1997; (c) under a court order or as required
-- by law; (d) "for the purposes of hospital administration or bona fide medical research"; (e) with the consent of the person to whom
-- it relates; (f) where the disclosure would be privileged. (3) $10,000 or 12 months.
DECLARE Disclosure IS ONE OF
    `a news report naming the donor`
    `a social media post naming the recipient`
    `enforcing the Act`
    `a complaint about a doctor under the Medical Registration Act`
    `a court order`
    `bona fide medical research`
    `with the consent of the person concerned`
    `a privileged communication`

GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A Disclosure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the disclosure is an offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the disclosure`
    WHEN `a news report naming the donor` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a social media post naming the recipient` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE
